## Current Engine Target

- Current target engine: Unreal Engine 5.6.1 installed at `C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6`.
- Current default UnrealMCP editor bridge port: `127.0.0.1:55561`. Keep this distinct from the older UE 5.7 MCP bridge on `55557`; use `UNREAL_MCP_5_6_1_PORT` or `-UnrealMCPPort=` only when an explicit override is needed. Do not use generic `UNREAL_MCP_PORT` for this fork.
- `MCPGameProject/MCPGameProject.uproject` should use `EngineAssociation` `5.6`; its Target.cs files should use UE 5.6 compatible build settings/include order.
- Keep every PCG plugin shipped with UE_5.6 enabled in `MCPGameProject`: `PCG`, `PCGBiomeCore`, `PCGBiomeSample`, `PCGExternalDataInterop`, `PCGGeometryScriptInterop`, `PCGInstancedActorsInterop`, `PCGNiagaraInterop`, and `PCGWaterInterop`.
- Preserve UE 5.6 compatibility guards for APIs introduced or changed in UE 5.7: material resource shader lookup, PCG pin current-type reporting, Niagara default-binding and enabled-renderer helpers, static mesh render LOD export, Nanite settings accessors, ControlRig blueprint headers, animation transition settings, and BlendSpace sample single-frame fields.
- When UE 5.7-only data cannot be read under UE 5.6.1, return a stable fallback value plus an `unavailable_in_ue_5_6` note instead of removing the JSON key.
- Android packaging is out of scope for the current UE 5.6.1 compatibility pass unless the user explicitly re-enables it.

## ControlRig Authoring Module

- ControlRig recipe authoring now lives inside the existing UnrealMCP plugin as the editor-only module `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`.
- The editor subsystem is `UUnrealMCPControlRigAuthoringSubsystem`; Python adapters should prefer this subsystem through Unreal Python/reflection and may keep only a short legacy fallback for already-running old editor sessions.
- Do not create a second ControlRig authoring plugin alongside UnrealMCP. Main `UnrealMCP` C++ bridge code must not include or statically depend on `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`; use reflection/Python boundaries for authoring calls.
- Generated ControlRig, AnimBP, and content assets must still load, compile, cook, package, and run with the UnrealMCP plugin disabled or absent unless the user explicitly approves that dependency.

