## Project Systems (Authored Content)

- MCPWeather — camera-following rain/snow weather manager (BP + MPC + material functions + Niagara). Durable doc: `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/systems/mcpweather.md`. Assets live under `/Game/MCPWeather` (`MCPGameProject/Content/MCPWeather`) and are self-contained (no UltraDynamicSky or other external `/Game` content dependency; engine refs only). BP `RainFX`/`SnowFX` → `FX/Rain/NS_MCPWeather_Rain` / `FX/Snow/NS_MCPWeather_Snow`; `SetWeather` drives `MPC_MCPWeather` + Niagara `User.Amount`.
- Anime SkyDome — 서브컬처풍 TOD 스카이돔 (M_AnimeSky 마스터 머티리얼 + BP_AnimeSkyDome). Durable doc: `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/systems/anime-skydome.md`. Assets live under `/Game/Sky` (`MCPGameProject/Content/Sky`), engine-asset dependencies only (no UnrealMCP references).
- Other authored-system, study, and review docs for this project are indexed in `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/README.md`.

## SkyDome Panorama Converter Dependency Check

- For SkyDome panorama converter planning, implementation, or verification, first check `Python/README.md`, `Python/pyproject.toml`, and `Python/uv.lock`.
- Also apply `codex/docs/workflows/skydome-panorama-converter.md`.
- The initial converter is a no-C++ editor-only project plugin under `MCPGameProject/Plugins/SkyDomeTools`. Do not add a `MCPGameProject.uproject` plugin entry by default; rely on the plugin descriptor for default editor loading. Keep the descriptor `EditorOnly` and keep PythonScriptPlugin limited to the editor target so packaging does not include the tool as runtime content. Unreal Python is only the menu wrapper; the converter and Tkinter UI run externally through `uv --directory .\Python ...`. The approved VDB preview exception is a narrow editor-only `SkyDomeTools` C++ helper that applies Sparse Volume Texture frame transforms to Heterogeneous Volume components because Unreal Python exposes that property as read-only; do not expand this into runtime modules or gameplay/component dependencies.
- The initial converter dependency set is Pillow plus NumPy. Do not add OpenCV, EXR/HDR libraries, Unreal import/material dependencies, C++ modules, build dependencies, or engine/build-version checks unless the current task actually implements and justifies those phases.
- Use the pinned Python 3.11 environment for `uv --directory .\Python ...` commands. If `uv` selects Python 3.12, 3.14, or newer, rerun with `--python 3.11` before diagnosing package failures.
- Treat Unreal Editor's embedded Python, currently expected around Python 3.11.8 for UE 5.6, as a separate runtime. The first converter pass should run as an external CLI; later Unreal Python UI/tools should call that CLI instead of importing Pillow/NumPy inside the engine Python.
- For scripted Unreal image texture imports through `AssetImportTask`, apply the Interchange guard in `codex/docs/workflows/unreal-asset-authoring.md` before import and restore the previous CVar values afterward. Do not apply that bypass to OpenVDB/Sparse Volume Texture import, which relies on UE 5.6's Interchange OpenVDB path.
- For polar UV cloud modularization, apply `Docs/Tools/skydome_polar_cloud_layout.md`: start from the supplied polar UV texture, extract cloud modules, place Unreal card actors, and validate a viewport screenshot before any Hunyuan mesh generation. Hunyuan should generate detailed geometry only; texture generation is out of scope for that phase.

## Verification

- For Python changes, run:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python -m py_compile unreal_mcp_server.py tools\tool_discovery.py tools\tool_policy.py tools\management_tools.py tools\mutation_result_contract.py tools\python_tools.py tools\pcg_tools.py services\unreal_bridge_connection.py
uv --directory .\Python run python -c "import unreal_mcp_server; print('server import ok')"
uvx ruff check --select F821 .\Python\tools .\Python\services .\Python\scripts .\Python\unreal_mcp_server.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\smoke_tool_registration.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\mcp_tool_parity_audit.py --fail-on issues
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_management_tools.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_tool_policy_contract.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_mutation_result_contract.py
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\test_tool_discovery_contract.py
