```

- C++ plugin verification should use the current target engine at `C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6` unless the user explicitly changes the target.
- The standard build command is:

```powershell
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat' MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development -Project="$Project" -WaitMutex
```

- Avoid kicking off a full source-engine rebuild unless necessary or explicitly requested.
